== Reception ==
Fans on social media criticised the thirteenth series, including the following aspects of the final week: time limit as too short, tasks as heavily complex within time allowed, bakes as short on quality, and judges' perceived overly negative comments.<ref>{{cite news |first=Katie |last=Archer |date=16 November 2022 |title=''Bake Off'' fans complain final was ruined by judges asking too much in too little time |url=https://news.yahoo.com/bake-off-fans-complain-final-ruined-judges-too-much-too-little-time-104844161.html |website=[[Yahoo! Entertainment]] UK |access-date=16 November 2022 }}</ref>

Besides what fans noted, Nicola Austin of ''[[Digital Spy]]'' further criticised the series's Technical challenges as the production's intentions for amateur bakers "to fail", highlight one-step instruction, "Make a lemon meringue pie", for week five's (Dessert) "Lemon Meringue Pie"; and lack of instructions to properly use vegetarian [[gelatin]] for the finale's "Summer Pudding Bombe". Austin further stated, "[M]uch of the judges' precise specifications, timings and presentation requirements now lean more towards professional standards," different from what ''Bake Off'' initially intended to be. She further criticised the series's "stereotypical presentation of Mexican culture" in episode five and other "faux pas on display", like Halloween-themed bakes in episode six and [[spring roll]]s as a Technical challenge.<ref>{{cite news |first=Nicola |last=Austin |date=17 November 2022 |title=The Great British Bake Off needs to fix this big problem before it returns |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a41988816/great-british-bake-off-controversy-backlash/ |website=[[Digital Spy]] |access-date=19 November 2022 }}</ref>

In response to the fan backlash, especially toward the Mexican Week, the producers' decision not to produce nationality-themed challenges for the following fourteenth series was made although this was met with further backlash from TV chef Antony Worrall Thompson.<ref>{{cite magazine |first=Celeste |last=McCauley |date=3 September 2023 |title=''The Great British Baking Show'' Eliminates Theme Weeks After Accusations of Racism |url=https://people.com/the-great-british-baking-show-makes-changes-ahead-of-season-premiere-7965067 |magazine=[[People (magazine)|People]] |access-date=6 September 2023 }}</ref>

Contestant Dawn Hollyoak died on 5 July 2024, aged 61, with Hollywood and Leith leading tributes.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cd17ezpw04lo|title=Great British Bake Off's Dawn Hollyoak dies aged 61|work=[[BBC News]]|date=6 July 2024|access-date=7 July 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://metro.co.uk/2024/07/06/great-british-bake-off-star-dawn-hollyoak-dies-aged-61-21175810/|title=Great British Bake Off star Dawn Hollyoak dies aged 61|last=Lawes|first=Ruth|work=[[Metro (British newspaper)|Metro]]|date=6 July 2024|access-date=7 July 2024}}</ref>

